# Required: server-side only, never exposed to the browser.
# The /api/generate route reads this to call the Gemini API. Get a free key
# at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (this is a *generative AI* key —
# different from the OAuth Client ID/Secret used for "Sign in with Google",
# which can't be used here).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override which Gemini model /api/generate calls. Google renames
# and retires model IDs fairly often — if generation starts failing with a
# 404, check the current recommended model at
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models and set it here without
# needing a code change.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Required: Supabase (real auth + persisted history).
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Project Settings → API Keys → "Publishable and secret API keys" tab.
#    (Supabase renamed these in 2025-2026: "publishable key" replaces what
#    used to be called the "anon key", and "secret key" replaces
#    "service_role key". If your project still shows the old names, use
#    anon → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and
#    service_role → SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY instead — same values, same
#    slots below, it doesn't matter which naming your project shows you.)
# 3. Paste the Project URL and the publishable key (starts sb_publishable_,
#    or the old anon key, a long eyJ... JWT) here. Safe to expose to the
#    browser — row-level security is what actually protects the data, not
#    secrecy of this key. See supabase/schema.sql for the RLS policies.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The secret key (starts sb_secret_, or the old service_role key, also a
# long eyJ... JWT) from the same page. This one bypasses row-level security
# entirely — never expose it to the browser, never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. If you don't see one yet, look for a "Create new API keys"
# or "Generate secret key" button on that page. Only used server-side in
# app/api/account/delete/route.ts, to delete a user's own auth.users row
# (something the publishable/anon key can't do).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional: Upstash Redis, for real distributed rate limiting on
# /api/generate. Without these, the app still works — it falls back to a
# simple in-memory limiter (see lib/rateLimit.ts), which is fine for local
# development and single-instance deployments but won't hold up correctly
# across multiple serverless instances.
# 1. Create a free database at https://console.upstash.com (Redis → Create
#    Database — the free tier is generous enough for this).
# 2. On the database's page, copy the "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL" and
#    "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN" values shown under the REST API section.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Not wired up yet. See README "Next steps" for what each of these is for. ---

# Stripe (metered/usage-based billing) — https://stripe.com
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STRIPE_METERED_PRICE_ID=
